learnings:
  - 'Green repo tests do not prove a release: smoke-test the packed tarball and the published package from a fresh npm install in an empty folder'
  - The global atelier is a pnpm link to the repo dist and hides packaging bugs
  - npm renames any .gitignore inside a package to .npmignore - ship templates as dotless gitignore
  - 'Publish with pnpm publish (workspace: deps) and --no-git-checks when only .paradigm state is dirty'
  - A core command must not depend on an optional peer (render needed node-canvas)
  - Two on-disk formats (v1/v2 workspace manifest) need one reader that knows both
  - Origin checks must use the port the server actually bound - Vite strictPort:false moves ports silently
  - ffmpeg palettegen stats_mode=single needs paletteuse new=1 or every GIF frame uses frame 0's palette
  - .purpose anchors must be recomputed from the code they pin - offset refreshes drift
  - Look at rendered output (late frames and file size) - a valid file can still be blank
  - npm registry can take minutes to show a publish - poll before declaring failure
